WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.640
It’s kind of farfetched [a terrorist attack].

2
00:00:02.640 --> 00:00:15.860
But hey, man, nothing today . . . I could see anything trying to happen, or happening, with these people [ISIS].

3
00:00:15.860 --> 00:00:26.660
That would be a great target, if they hit one of those industries here, because it would be a chain reaction.

4
00:00:26.660 --> 00:00:35.460
The government, or whatever you call it, security, it’s going to have to tighten up.

5
00:00:35.460 --> 00:00:44.280
And if you in there close by . . . We’re not really safe where we at here [in Moss Bluff].

6
00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:57.550
But we’re much safer than we were in Mossville . . . from the leaks and . . . because there’ve been times that we had leaks and we had to stay in and the alarm went off,

7
00:00:57.550 --> 00:01:02.270
and you had to stay . . . what they call that?

8
00:01:02.270 --> 00:01:04.630
Shut in.

9
00:01:04.630 --> 00:01:07.350
Where you had to stay in your house and turn off all your . . .

10
00:01:07.350 --> 00:01:10.150
What plant was leaking?

11
00:01:10.150 --> 00:01:17.750
Vista, Georgia Gulf . . . explosions.

12
00:01:17.750 --> 00:01:21.870
And I think PPG a couple of times, and . . .

13
00:01:21.870 --> 00:01:23.670
Was it ever Axiall?

14
00:01:23.670 --> 00:01:30.290
Yeah, well, PPG that’s the old Axiall.

15
00:01:30.290 --> 00:01:34.530
It was PPG at that time.

16
00:01:34.530 --> 00:01:43.970
And since Axiall have had it, there have been a couple of incidents where they had a shelter in place.

17
00:01:43.970 --> 00:01:54.570
Because they had the big speakers throughout the community down there, and they would come on when they had something in the area.

18
00:01:54.570 --> 00:02:05.070
Conoco, Olin, or some of them would have a chemical leak, a train car derailment or something.

19
00:02:05.070 --> 00:02:08.750
They had a warning system and it helped.

20
00:02:08.750 --> 00:02:17.970
Most of the wind comes out of the south and the southwest and everything.

21
00:02:17.970 --> 00:02:32.070
And the way Mossville was situated there, it was kind of fully almost surrounded by industry, some type of industry.

22
00:02:32.070 --> 00:02:43.310
Not all chemical, because the electrical thing was to the north and Citgo and Firestone, PPG, and all of that to the south.

23
00:02:43.310 --> 00:02:53.350
To the east you had Conoco and Georgia Gulf and old Sasol was Vista.

24
00:02:53.350 --> 00:02:58.690
And, you know, it was pretty well locked in.

25
00:02:58.690 --> 00:03:04.210
It [the buyout] gave me a chance to get out of the boat.

26
00:03:04.210 --> 00:03:05.250
You understand?

27
00:03:05.250 --> 00:03:12.870
My grandfather used to say, “You’ve got too much in the boat, sooner or later it’s going to run over.

28
00:03:12.870 --> 00:03:15.230
You’re going to have some spills.

29
00:03:15.230 --> 00:03:18.230
So if you get a chance to get out of there, get out of there.”

30
00:03:18.230 --> 00:03:21.670
So what would happen when the alarms went off?

31
00:03:21.670 --> 00:03:25.350
Well, they would say shelter in place.

32
00:03:25.350 --> 00:03:29.810
A lot of times they shut all the traffic down coming through.

33
00:03:29.810 --> 00:03:37.550
Just depending on what kind of spill or release they had, how long or what.

34
00:03:37.550 --> 00:03:43.850
And there’s times they’ve shut the interstate down.

35
00:03:43.850 --> 00:03:46.050
Depending on which way the wind’s blowing, too,

36
00:03:46.050 --> 00:04:07.110
they’d shut the interstate down or you had to stay in your house and turn off all the . . . your air conditions and stuff because of the suction of . . . A lot of people got sick over it.

37
00:04:07.110 --> 00:04:08.630
You got caught in the wrong place.

38
00:04:08.630 --> 00:04:21.530
And if you in transit there and you’re passing by there and there’s chlorine, formalin or whatever the leak was, it’d get you.

39
00:04:21.530 --> 00:04:24.290
A lot of people had to go to the emergency rooms and stuff.

40
00:04:24.290 --> 00:04:29.810
But like they say, “Oh, it’s not that bad.”

41
00:04:29.810 --> 00:04:33.950
But if it’s bad enough to shut the interstate down, like he said.

42
00:04:33.950 --> 00:04:39.390
Grandfather used to say, “Too much of anything that kills will kill you.”

43
00:04:39.390 --> 00:04:42.170
If it kills something, too much of it will kill you.
